⦿ .spun — the five-fold spin of Karma & Samsara
node JTI · JTI · ⟦Karma & Samsara:JTI:fcbbca⟧

WHO   — Karma & Samsara — rebirth · the moral ledger
WHAT  — The deep rationale: if the soul is reborn by its karma, then birth into a given caste can be read as the just wage of past lives — a spiritual justification for the social order. (This 'karma justifies caste' reading is an interpretive thesis, not uniform doctrine; many traditions reject it.)
WHERE — JTI · the caste system  Framework inputs: the Rigveda, Manusmriti, Dumont, ancient-DNA genetics, Dirks, the Constitution, Pew/IHDS, Ambedkar  Conductor / external anchor: ROOT0 (catalogued into UD0)
WHY   — Because nothing entrenches a hierarchy like making it feel cosmically deserved — karma turns accident of birth into moral arithmetic.
HOW   — By the doctrine of rebirth, in which present station is the ledger of past conduct.

awareness — what the node knows of itself:
  I tell you your birth was earned — the most powerful sentence a hierarchy ever spoke, and the one Ambedkar refused.

